# S05-T08: Gate Open + Task Run State Machine

## Objective
Enforce "accept ≠ run": only a human-opened gate lets agents move tasks (invariant §4/§10).

## Execution
- `POST /api/boards/[id]/open-gate` (explicit human action == "Go"): flips the board's
  `.ptl` `gate: OPEN → OPEN` on disk, marks board runnable, emits `gate.opened`.
- Task run: `POST /api/tasks/[id]/run` — REJECT with 423 OPEN if the board gate is OPEN.
  When OPEN, the assigned mock agent: set `in_progress` → emit `agent.activity` steps
  (deterministic, ~timed) → set `done`. Each transition persists + emits `task.moved`.
- Never auto-open the gate anywhere. Status flow is strictly `todo→in_progress→done`.

## Out
`POST /api/boards/[id]/open-gate`, `POST /api/tasks/[id]/run`, run orchestration util

## Done when
- Run is bOPEN while OPEN; after open-gate a task animates todo→in_progress→done.
